# Append to /root/caddy/Caddyfile on the Hetzner host, then reload:
#   docker exec caddy-caddy-1 caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# Caddy also needs the media directory mounted, alongside the p4td one:
#   - /root/mojo-dog-grooming/media:/srv/mojo-media:ro
#
# The Hetzner cloud firewall only allows 80 and 443, so the app must go
# through Caddy — binding the container to a high port directly is
# unreachable from outside.

# app.mojoandco.uk is the real home and what new builds point at. The sslip.io
# name is the interim one it ran on before the A record existed, and it is
# still listed here on purpose: every TestFlight build already on a phone has
# https://mojo.178-104-29-66.sslip.io/api compiled into it, so dropping the
# name would black those installs out with no way to recover but reinstalling.
#
# Both names on one site block rather than a redirect from the old to the new:
# the clients are API callers, not browsers, and a redirect changes POST
# semantics for anything that does not follow it exactly.
#
# Retire the sslip name once no build in the wild still points at it — that
# means a release out and adopted, not merely cut. Removing it also needs
# DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS on the host trimmed to match.
app.mojoandco.uk, mojo.178-104-29-66.sslip.io {
    handle_path /media/* {
        root * /srv/mojo-media
        file_server
    }
    reverse_proxy 172.17.0.1:8010
    encode gzip
}
